        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Anna Maria, Florida; Anna Maria Island; Bradenton Beach, Florida; Redfish Pass\n- Organizations: Manatee County\n- Water bodies: Gulf of Mexico; Longboat Pass; Longboat Key; Anna Maria Sound; Tampa Bay; Pine Island Sound\n\nFacts:\n- Anna Maria, Florida, is a city in Manatee County, Florida, United States.\n- Anna Maria, Florida, occupies the northern part of Anna Maria Island and is one of three municipalities on the island.\n- Anna Maria Island is bounded on the west by the Gulf of Mexico, on the south by Longboat Pass, on the east by Anna Maria Sound, and on the north by Tampa Bay.\n- Longboat Pass separates Anna Maria Island from Longboat Key.\n- Bradenton Beach, Florida, is a city on Anna Maria Island in Manatee County, Florida, United States.\n- Redfish Pass is a strait in Florida that connects Pine Island Sound with the Gulf of Mexico.",
